===Pronunciation===
* {{a|GenAm}} {{IPA|en|/ˌɡɹæd͡ʒuˈeɪʃən/}}
* {{a|RP}} {{IPA|en|/ˌɡɹædjuˈeɪʃən/}}
* {{rhymes|en|eɪʃən|s=4}}
* {{audio|en|En-uk-graduation.oga|Audio (UK)}}

===Noun===
{{en-noun|~}}

# The action or process of [[graduate|graduating]] and receiving a diploma for completing a course of study (such as from an [[educational institution]]).
#: {{ux|en|The '''graduation''' ball was the students' chance to say goodbye to each other.}}
#: {{ux|en|After my '''graduation''', I took a year out to travel, then went into an office job.}}
# A [[commencement]] ceremony.
# {{lb|en|Japanese entertainment}} The action or process of leaving a group.
#: {{ux|en|'''graduation''' from {{w|AKB48}}}}
# {{lb|en|sciences}} A marking (e.g., on a container) indicating a measurement on a [[scale]], usually one of many such markings.
# The exposure of a liquid in large surfaces to the air, so as to hasten its evaporation.

